spire%20One%20ZG5%20motherboard%20DA0ZG5MB8F0%20-%20top%20view.jpg"},{"title":"Acer Aspire One ZG5 motherboard DA0ZG5MB8F0 - bottom view.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Acer_Aspire_One_ZG5_motherboard_DA0ZG5MB8F0_-_bottom_view.jpg/500px-Acer_Aspire_One_ZG5_motherboard_DA0ZG5MB8F0_-_bottom_view.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","original":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0b/Acer_Aspire_One_ZG5_motherboard_DA0ZG5MB8F0_-_bottom_view.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","w":3720,"h":2220,"mime":"image/jpeg","size":4638271,"desc":"The reverse side of the motherboard for the Acer Aspire One ZG5. This view clearly shows the integrated Intel Atom N270 processor, single DDR2 RAM slot and ZIF connector for the keyboard. This side also features two separate card reader slots: the main SD card slot on the motherboard itself (right) and a \"Storage Expansion\" slot on the I/O daughterboard (left)DA0ZG5PB6E0, from which booting is not supported by the standard BIOS. Also visible are the single DDR2 RAM slot and the \"HannStar J MV-4\" marking from the PCB manufacturer","cats":"Self-published work|Netbook motherboards|Disassembled Acer Aspire One|Acer Aspire One 110/150|Files by User:Siarhei V|Photos of Laptops taken by User:Siarhei V","creator":"Siarhei Besarab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Acer%20Aspire%20One%20ZG5%20motherboard%20DA0ZG5MB8F0%20-%20bottom%20view.jpg"}],"error":null}